  ex:l7-next-17-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "The sum from individual departures agrees with the sum of the two components: 114 pp²."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-17-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Complete the decomposition"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-17-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-17-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Does the variation add up? The total sum of squares is 114 squared percentage points, exactly equal to 84 between methods plus 30 within methods."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-17-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "Complete the decomposition"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-next-17-cards-1, ex:l7-next-17-cards-2, ex:l7-next-17-cards-3, ex:l7-next-17-cards-4 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-17-cards-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Total variation"@en ; cd:body "Directly from 18 observations: SS = 114 squared percentage points; df = 17."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-17-cards-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Between methods"@en ; cd:body "SS = 84 squared percentage points; df = 2."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-17-cards-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Within methods"@en ; cd:body "SS = 30 squared percentage points; df = 15."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-17-cards-4 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Accounting check"@en ; cd:body "84 + 30 = 114, and 2 + 15 = 17; significance still requires a reference model."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-18-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "What do the 18 recoveries tell us?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-18-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "F = 21 and p ≈ 0.000045 give evidence that at least one method has a different mean recovery."@en ; cd:interpretsResource ex:level7-anova-read-table ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-18-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Read an ANOVA table"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-18-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-18-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "How does the table produce F? The variation between methods is large relative to the variation within methods."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-read-table a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Annotated one-way ANOVA table"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-read-table.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "One-way ANOVA for river-water recovery. Between methods: SS 84, df 2, MS 42, F 21, p 0.00004484. Within methods: SS 30, df 15, MS 2. Total: SS 114, df 17. SS shows where recovery varies and df records how many independent deviations each source contributes. MS compares variation per degree of freedom between and within methods. F compares those two scales. The small p-value shows that an F this large or larger would be rare under equal means."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-read-table .
  ex:level7-anova-factorial-grid a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Build a 3 by 2 factorial design"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-factorial-grid.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Three methods crossed with two water matrices, six independent preparations per combination. Stage one marks the existing river-water experiment and stage two adds wastewater, making 36 preparations."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-factorial-grid .
  ex:level7-anova-marginal-means a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Read the two marginal averages"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-marginal-means.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Mean recoveries by matrix for Method A are 94 and 92, for B 98 and 86, for C 93 and 94. Marginals over matrices are 93, 92 and 93.5. Marginals over methods are 95 percent for river water and 90.67 percent for wastewater."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-marginal-means .
  ex:level7-anova-model-components a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "What the two-way model fits"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-model-components.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "In R formula notation, A star B includes the method main effect, the water matrix main effect, and their interaction. For B in river water, the additive prediction is 94.17 percent. Adding the interaction gives the fitted mean of 98.00 percent. An observed 98.06 percent leaves a residual of 0.06 percentage points."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-model-components .
  ex:level7-anova-two-way-table a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Read the two-way ANOVA table"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-two-way-table.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Top table with interaction. Method: SS 14, df 2, MS 7, F 3.5, p 0.0430. Matrix: SS 169, df 1, MS 169, F 84.5, p 3.13 times ten to the minus ten. Method by matrix: SS 278, df 2, MS 139, F 69.5, p 5.48 times ten to the minus twelve. Residual: SS 60, df 30, MS 2. Total: SS 521, df 35. Bottom additive table. Method: SS 14, df 2, MS 7, F 0.663, p 0.5224. Matrix: SS 169, df 1, MS 169, F 16, p 0.000350. Residual: SS 338, df 32, MS 10.5625. Total: SS 521, df 35."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-two-way-table .
  ex:level7-anova-review-cases a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Choose the analysis for each design"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-review-cases.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Three independent methods in one matrix with comparable error variances suggest one-way ANOVA. Crossing methods with matrix suggests two-way ANOVA with interaction. Comparing means under unequal variances suggests Welch ANOVA."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-review-cases .
  ex:level7-anova-tukey-interval a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Build a Tukey interval"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-tukey-interval.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "B minus A is 98 minus 94, or 4.00 percentage points. Residual MS is 2, with six preparations per group, giving sqrt(2 divided by 6) = 0.577 pp. The studentized-range 95th percentile for three means and 15 residual degrees of freedom is 3.673. Multiply by 0.577 to get the half-width 2.12. The simultaneous interval is [1.88, 6.12]."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-tukey-interval .
  ex:level7-anova-more-factors a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "What changes with a third factor?"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-more-factors.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Crossing three methods, two matrices, and two temperatures makes twelve conditions. Three-way interaction asks whether the method-by-matrix interaction changes with temperature."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-more-factors .
  ex:level7-anova-pool-ranks a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Pool recoveries before ranking"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-pool-ranks.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Ordered recoveries are 81 from A, 84 from A, 84 from B, 88 from B, 90 from C and 92 from C. The two 84s share ranks 2 and 3 and each receives 2.5. Rank sums are 3.5 for A, 6.5 for B and 11 for C."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-pool-ranks .
  ex:level7-anova-two-way-observations a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Six method–matrix combinations"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-two-way-observations.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Thirty-six synthetic recovery measurements arranged by water matrix and preparation method. Each method and matrix combination has six measurements. Means in river water are 94, 98, and 93 percent. Means in wastewater are 92, 86, and 94 percent."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-two-way-observations .
  ex:level7-anova-two-way-ss a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Partition the two-way sums of squares"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-two-way-ss.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "The total sum of squares of 521 divides into method SS 14, matrix SS 169, and additive residual SS 338. The method and matrix contributions use weighted deviations of marginal means from the grand mean. The residual sums squared deviations of individual recoveries from their additive predictions."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-two-way-ss .
  ex:level7-anova-two-way-interpretation a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Interpret the interaction before the averages"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-two-way-interpretation.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "B averages 92 percent and A 93 percent across both matrices. The B-minus-A comparison is +4 percentage points in river water and −6 in wastewater. The interaction test supports a change in the contrast across water matrices. Individual pair differences require their own uncertainty estimates."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-two-way-interpretation .
  ex:level7-anova-additive-fit a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Fit an additive two-way model"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-additive-fit.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "The grand mean is 92.83 percent. Method B has a marginal mean of 92 percent, a shift of minus 0.83 percentage points. River water averages 95 percent, a shift of plus 2.17 points. Adding the two shifts to the grand mean gives a predicted 94.17 percent for Method B in river water, calculated from unrounded means."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-additive-fit .
  ex:level7-anova-additive-table a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Build the additive ANOVA table"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-additive-table.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Additive ANOVA table. Method: SS 14, df 2, MS 7, F 0.663, p 0.5224, eta squared 2.69%. Matrix: SS 169, df 1, MS 169, F 16, p 0.000350, eta squared 32.44%. Residual: SS 338, df 32, MS 10.5625. Total: SS 521, df 35. Eta squared is the share of total SS associated with each factor."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-additive-table .
  ex:level7-anova-additive-grouped-recoveries a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Compare the two groupings"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-additive-grouped-recoveries.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "The same 36 recoveries appear in both plots. Grouped by method, the means are A 93, B 92, and C 93.50 percent. Grouped by water matrix, the means are 95 percent for river water and 90.67 percent for wastewater. Circles represent river water and squares represent wastewater. Color identifies the method. The additive model gives p 0.5224 for method and p 0.000350 for matrix."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-additive-grouped-recoveries .
  ex:level7-anova-operator-design a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Who processed the samples?"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-operator-design.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Hypothetical assignment of the 18 river-water samples. X processes three samples with method A and three with B. Y processes three with B and three with C. Z processes three with C and three with A. Each operator uses two methods, giving an incomplete block design."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-operator-design .
  ex:level7-anova-operator-grouping a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Same recoveries, two one-way analyses"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-operator-grouping.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Both dot plots contain the same 18 river-water observations. By method the means are 94, 98, and 93 percent; p is approximately 0.00004484 and eta squared is 73.7 percent. By hypothetical operator the means are 95.93, 95.60, and 93.48 percent; p is 0.214 and eta squared is 18.6 percent. Color identifies the method in both plots."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-operator-grouping .
  ex:level7-anova-operator-adjusted a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Allow for both method and operator"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-operator-adjusted.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "In the additive model with both factors, testing method after accounting for operator gives p approximately 0.000633 and partial eta squared 67.8 percent. Testing operator after accounting for method gives p approximately 0.974 and partial eta squared 0.4 percent. Adding operator to a method-only model reduces residual SS from 30.00 to 29.88."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-operator-adjusted .
  ex:level7-anova-model-prediction a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "One measurement and one prediction"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-model-prediction.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Six measured recoveries from method B in river water. Preparation 3 measured 98.06 percent. The model predicts 94.17 percent for all six: the overall mean of 92.83 percent, minus 0.83 percentage points for method B, plus 2.17 percentage points for river water. Its residual, observed minus fitted, is 3.89 percentage points."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-model-prediction .
  ex:level7-anova-model-system a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Six predictions from shared parameters"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-model-system.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "The prediction for each combination adds a grand mean, a method shift and a matrix shift. The grand mean is 92.83 percent and the method B shift is minus 0.83 percentage points. River water adds 2.17 points and wastewater subtracts 2.17 points. The fitted values, using unrounded terms, are 94.17 and 89.83 percent. All 36 measurements inform the shared parameters."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-model-system .
  ex:level7-anova-model-pattern a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Where does the additive fit miss?"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-model-pattern.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "The additive model predicts a B-minus-A gap of minus one percentage point in both matrices. The observed gap is plus four in river water and minus six in wastewater. The departures from the predicted gap are plus five and minus five percentage points, respectively."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-model-pattern .
