  ex:l7-next-19-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Place F on the null distribution"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-19-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "For the original data, F = 21 and the right-tail probability is about 0.00004484. The table shows the result for the current slider settings."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-19-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Place F on the null distribution"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-19-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-19-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Why does F = 21 give a small p-value? Under the null hypothesis and classical model assumptions, the right-tail probability beyond F = 21 is approximately 0.00004484."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-20-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Check the sampling and error model"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-20-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "The classical F reference requires independent experimental units, an appropriate mean model, common error variance, and normally distributed errors."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-20-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Check the sampling and error model"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-20-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-20-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "When is the classical F test justified? The classical F reference requires independent experimental units, an appropriate mean model, common error variance, and normally distributed errors."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-20-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "Check the sampling and error model"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-next-20-cards-1, ex:l7-next-20-cards-2, ex:l7-next-20-cards-3, ex:l7-next-20-cards-4 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-20-cards-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Independent units"@en ; cd:body "Six injections of one preparation are not six independent preparation replicates."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-20-cards-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Appropriate mean model"@en ; cd:body "Method means describe expected recovery; errors are centered on zero."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-20-cards-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Classical error assumptions"@en ; cd:body "Independent errors, common variance, and normal errors support the exact F reference."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-20-cards-4 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Schematic, not evidence"@en ; cd:body "Illustrative residual patterns explain assumptions; they are not observed findings."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-21-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "What do the residuals tell us?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-21-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Look for systematic departures from the Q–Q line, especially at the ends, when assessing whether normal errors are plausible."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-21-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Diagnose the residuals"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-21-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-21-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "What can residual plots reveal? In a normal Q-Q plot, look for systematic departures from the reference line."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-21-visual a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Diagnose the residuals"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-21.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "A residual is observed recovery minus the fitted method mean. The table lists all 18 river-water preparations with observed recovery, fitted recovery, and residual. The normal Q-Q plot of these residuals compares the ordered decimal residuals with a normal reference line. In the schematic heavy-tail example, both ends depart strongly: the left tail falls far below the line and the right tail rises far above it. The descriptive KS distances to separate fitted normal distributions are 0.110 for the river-water residuals and 0.248 for the heavy-tail example. The Monte Carlo p-values are approximately 0.812 and 0.040, respectively, with model fitting repeated on each simulated sample."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-22-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "How much squared variation does method account for?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-22-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Method accounts for 84 of 114 units of observed squared variation, or 73.7%."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-22-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "How much variation is explained?"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-22-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-22-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Does statistical significance imply practical importance? Eta squared is approximately 0.737 in this sample, but practical importance requires recovery specifications and differences expressed in percentage points."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-22-visual a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "How much variation is explained?"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-22.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Using only the grand mean leaves 114 squared percentage points of residual spread. Using three method means leaves 30. The observed reduction of 84 divided by 114 is 73.7 percent."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-22-formula a cd:MathExpression ; skos:prefLabel "How much variation is explained?"@en ; cd:body "How much variation is explained?"@en ; cd:latex "\\eta^2=\\frac{SS_B}{SS_T}=\\frac{84}{114}\\approx0.73684" ; dct:hasPart ex:l7-next-22-legend ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-22-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-next-22-legend-1, ex:l7-next-22-legend-2, ex:l7-next-22-legend-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-22-legend-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "η² and SS"@en ; cd:body "η² (eta squared) is the dimensionless share of observed variation attributed to the method factor. SS means sum of squared deviations; B is between methods and T is total."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-22-legend-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "84 and 114"@en ; cd:body "84 is the between-method SS; 114 is total SS. Both are in squared percentage points."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-22-legend-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Operations"@en ; cd:body "The fraction bars divide. The equals signs show exact equality. ≈ means approximately equal after rounding to 0.73684."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-23-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Report the method effect"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-23-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Report F, its degrees of freedom and p-value alongside η², then judge the recovery gaps against your analytical tolerance."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-23-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Report the finding without overclaiming"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-23-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-23-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "What can we responsibly report? Report the design, model, F statistic with degrees of freedom, p-value, and effect size without claiming that every method pair differs."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-23-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "Report the finding without overclaiming"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-next-23-cards-1, ex:l7-next-23-cards-2, ex:l7-next-23-cards-3, ex:l7-next-23-cards-4 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-23-cards-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Design and model"@en ; cd:body "Synthetic data; six independent preparations per method; classical fixed-effects one-way ANOVA."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-23-cards-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Statistical result"@en ; cd:body "F(2, 15) = 21.0; p ≈ 4.48 × 10⁻⁵; eta squared = 0.737."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-23-cards-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Conditional global finding"@en ; cd:body "Evidence against equal population means, conditional on the design and error model."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-23-cards-4 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Next: controlled comparisons"@en ; cd:body "The global test identifies no specific pair and establishes no practical superiority."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-24-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Which pairs differ after ANOVA?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-24-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "The inferential target is the whole family of three pairs."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-24-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "A significant F leaves one question open"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-24-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-24-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Which methods actually differ? The significant omnibus ANOVA rejects equality of all three method means but does not identify which pairs differ."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-24-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "A significant F leaves one question open"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-next-24-cards-1, ex:l7-next-24-cards-2, ex:l7-next-24-cards-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-24-cards-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Overall result"@en ; cd:body "F(2, 15) = 21; p ≈ 0.00004484 in the synthetic one-way example."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-24-cards-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "What it establishes"@en ; cd:body "Reject equality of all three population means under the ANOVA assumptions."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-24-cards-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "What remains open"@en ; cd:body "A–B, A–C, and B–C require pairwise inference; the omnibus result does not locate differences."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-25-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "What is the largest gap we could see by chance?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-25-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Any pair can produce the largest gap under equal population means."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-25-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "A family of comparisons needs a rule"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-25-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-25-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "With equal population means, the largest sample mean gap can come from any pair. Standardize that maximum to build the Tukey reference."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-25-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "A family of comparisons needs a rule"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-next-25-cards-1, ex:l7-next-25-cards-2, ex:l7-next-25-cards-3, ex:l7-next-25-cards-4 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-25-cards-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Define the family"@en ; cd:body "Here, the family contains all three method comparisons: A–B, A–C, and B–C."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-25-cards-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Control the shared risk"@en ; cd:body "Family-wise error is the probability of at least one false positive in the family."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-25-cards-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "No automatic permission"@en ; cd:body "A significant omnibus F does not generally justify unadjusted pairwise p-values."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-25-cards-4 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Choose a suitable rule"@en ; cd:body "Tukey targets all pairwise mean comparisons; the family-wise error target here is 0.05."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Build a Tukey interval"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "The cutoff comes from the largest-gap distribution for all three methods."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Tukey HSD answers pairwise questions"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-26-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-tukey-interval-formula a cd:MathExpression ; skos:prefLabel "Tukey interval for equal group sizes"@en ; cd:body "Tukey interval for equal group sizes"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{aligned}\\Delta&=\\bar y_j-\\bar y_i\\\\h&=q_{1-\\alpha;k,\\nu}\\sqrt{\\frac{MS_W}{n}}\\\\\\text{Tukey interval}&=[\\Delta-h,\\,\\Delta+h]\\end{aligned}" ; dct:hasPart ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols-1, ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols-2, ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols-3, ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols-4 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Mean gap"@en ; cd:body "ȳⱼ and ȳᵢ are the sample mean recoveries (%) for methods j and i. Δ is the signed difference in percentage points (pp). For B minus A, j is B and i is A."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Error scale"@en ; cd:body "$MS_W$ is the residual mean square pooled across all methods, here 2 pp². n is the common sample size, here 6 independent preparations per method. The square root converts the variance of a single fitted mean to a standard error in pp."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Cutoff and width"@en ; cd:body "q is the studentized-range quantile at cumulative probability 1 − α. α is the family error level, here 0.05. k counts the methods (3) and ν is the residual degrees of freedom (15). h is the interval half-width in pp."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols-4 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Interval and notation"@en ; cd:body "The brackets give the lower and upper endpoints for the population mean difference. Subtract and add h to Δ. The fraction divides, juxtaposition multiplies, = denotes equality, and the superscript ² means squared."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-tukey-interval-formula, ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols, ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols-1, ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols-2, ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols-3, ex:l7-tukey-interval-symbols-4 .
  ex:l7-next-26-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "How does Tukey compare the pairs? For this balanced example, Tukey HSD uses the pooled within-group variance to give each pair a simultaneous interval half-width of 2.12083 percentage points."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table a cd:TableDefinition ; skos:prefLabel "Tukey HSD · 95% simultaneous intervals"@en ; cd:hasTableColumn ex:l7-next-26-table-col-1, ex:l7-next-26-table-col-2, ex:l7-next-26-table-col-3, ex:l7-next-26-table-col-4 ; cd:hasTableRow ex:l7-next-26-table-row-1, ex:l7-next-26-table-row-2, ex:l7-next-26-table-row-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-col-1 a cd:TableColumn ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Contrast"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-col-2 a cd:TableColumn ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Difference (pp)"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-col-3 a cd:TableColumn ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "95% interval (pp)"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-col-4 a cd:TableColumn ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Adjusted p"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-1 a cd:TableRow ; cd:position 1 ; cd:hasTableCell ex:l7-next-26-table-row-1-cell-1, ex:l7-next-26-table-row-1-cell-2, ex:l7-next-26-table-row-1-cell-3, ex:l7-next-26-table-row-1-cell-4 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-1-cell-1 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 1 ; cd:body "B − A"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-1-cell-2 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 2 ; cd:body "4"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-1-cell-3 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 3 ; cd:body "[1.88, 6.12]"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-1-cell-4 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 4 ; cd:body "0.000532"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-2 a cd:TableRow ; cd:position 2 ; cd:hasTableCell ex:l7-next-26-table-row-2-cell-1, ex:l7-next-26-table-row-2-cell-2, ex:l7-next-26-table-row-2-cell-3, ex:l7-next-26-table-row-2-cell-4 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-2-cell-1 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 1 ; cd:body "C − A"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-2-cell-2 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 2 ; cd:body "−1"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-2-cell-3 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 3 ; cd:body "[-3.12, 1.12]"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-2-cell-4 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 4 ; cd:body "0.457"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-3 a cd:TableRow ; cd:position 3 ; cd:hasTableCell ex:l7-next-26-table-row-3-cell-1, ex:l7-next-26-table-row-3-cell-2, ex:l7-next-26-table-row-3-cell-3, ex:l7-next-26-table-row-3-cell-4 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-3-cell-1 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 1 ; cd:body "C − B"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-3-cell-2 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 2 ; cd:body "−5"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-3-cell-3 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 3 ; cd:body "[-7.12, -2.88]"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-26-table-row-3-cell-4 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 4 ; cd:body "5.47e-05"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-27-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Read the post-hoc comparison plot"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-27-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "The intervals for B vs A and C vs B exclude zero."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-27-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Read the post-hoc comparison plot"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-27-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-27-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Which pairwise intervals exclude zero? The simultaneous 95% intervals exclude zero for B−A and C−B, but not for C−A."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-27-visual a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Read the post-hoc comparison plot"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-27.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "B minus A: 4, interval 1.88 to 6.12. C minus A: −1, interval −3.12 to 1.12. C minus B: −5, interval −7.12 to −2.88. Only C minus A crosses zero."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-28-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Holm: adjust the raw p-values"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-28-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Tukey builds simultaneous intervals. Holm adjusts a family of valid p-values."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-28-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Which follow-up method fits the question?"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-28-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-28-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Holm sorts the raw p-values, multiplies by the descending number of tests, and uses a running maximum capped at one."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-28-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "Which follow-up method fits the question?"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-next-28-cards-1, ex:l7-next-28-cards-2, ex:l7-next-28-cards-3, ex:l7-next-28-cards-4 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-28-cards-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "All pairs, common variance"@en ; cd:body "Use Tukey when all pairwise comparisons and its model assumptions match the question."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-28-cards-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Defined contrast family"@en ; cd:body "Holm or Bonferroni can control multiplicity for a specified family of valid contrast tests."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-28-cards-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Unequal variances"@en ; cd:body "Consider Games–Howell for pairwise inference, often alongside Welch's ANOVA."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-28-cards-4 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Planned does not mean gated"@en ; cd:body "Properly specified planned contrasts need not await a significant omnibus F test."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-29-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Fit one mean plus two factor effects"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-29-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "The additive model uses the same matrix shift for every method."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-29-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "A second factor changes the story"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-29-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-29-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Is the preferred method best in both matrices? The relative recovery of the methods depends on the water matrix, so a one-factor conclusion cannot automatically generalize."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-29-visual a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "A second factor changes the story"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-29.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Method means in percent, A 94 to 92, B 98 to 86, C 93 to 94, moving from river water to wastewater."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-30-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Add a second factor: water matrix"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-30-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Cross all three methods with both matrices."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-30-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Build a 3 × 2 factorial design"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-30-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-30-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "How do we cross methods with matrices? Testing all three methods in both matrices creates six combinations and, with six independent preparations per combination, 36 observations."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-30-table a cd:TableDefinition ; skos:prefLabel "Six independent preparations per combination"@en ; cd:hasTableColumn ex:l7-next-30-table-col-1, ex:l7-next-30-table-col-2, ex:l7-next-30-table-col-3, ex:l7-next-30-table-col-4 ; cd:hasTableRow ex:l7-next-30-table-row-1, ex:l7-next-30-table-row-2 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
