  ex:l7-next-32-table-row-2-cell-5 a cd:TableCell ; cd:position 5 ; cd:body "90.6667"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-33-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "When do two factors interact?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-33-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Interaction means the effect of one factor depends on the level of the other."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-33-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Interaction: the method effect depends on matrix"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-33-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-33-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "An interaction means the effect of one factor depends on the level of the other. Synergy and antagonism describe departures above and below an additive expectation for a chosen response and comparison."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-33-visual a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Interaction: the method effect depends on matrix"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-33.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "In the additive recovery model the p-values are 0.5224 for method and 0.000350 for water matrix. An interaction means the effect of one factor depends on the level of the other. In an illustrative plant experiment, a baseline mean growth of 10 cm, fertilizer effect of 4 cm, and extra-light effect of 3 cm give an additive expectation of 17 cm. Combined growth of 21 cm is synergistic, 4 cm above expectation. Combined growth of 14 cm is antagonistic, 3 cm below expectation."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-two-way-ss-formula a cd:MathExpression ; skos:prefLabel "Partition total variation in the balanced design"@en ; cd:body "Partition total variation in the balanced design"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{aligned}SS_T&=SS_M+SS_W+SS_E\\\\SS_E&=\\sum_{i,j,k}(y_{ijk}-\\hat y_{ij,\\mathrm{add}})^2\\end{aligned}" ; dct:hasPart ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend-1, ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend-2, ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend-3, ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend-4 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Indices and replication"@en ; cd:body "i indexes the three SPE methods, j the two water matrices, and k the six preparations within a combination. The sum runs over all combinations of these indices."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Recovery and fitted values"@en ; cd:body "$y_{ijk}$ is an observed recovery in percent. $\\hat{y}_{ij}$,add is its additive fitted value, using the grand mean plus the method and matrix shifts."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Sources of squared variation"@en ; cd:body "SSₜ is total SS, SSM is the method term, SSW is the water-matrix term, and SSE is the additive residual SS. Each is in squared percentage points."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend-4 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Operations"@en ; cd:body "Σ sums the indexed terms, plus adds, minus subtracts, parentheses group the residual, the superscript ² squares it, and = denotes equality."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-two-way-ss-formula, ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend, ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend-1, ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend-2, ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend-3, ex:l7-two-way-ss-legend-4 .
  ex:l7-next-34-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Partition the sums of squares"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-34-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "The additive fit separates method, matrix and residual variation."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-34-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Additive versus interacting effects"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-34-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-34-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Must interaction lines cross? Additive model profiles are parallel, whereas interacting mean profiles can be nonparallel without crossing."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-34-visual a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Additive versus interacting effects"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-34.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Method means in percent, A 94 to 92, B 98 to 86, C 93 to 94, moving from river water to wastewater. The comparison uses a hypothetical common shift of four points on the left."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Model the method–matrix interaction"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "A * B includes both main effects and their interaction."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "The two-way ANOVA model"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-35-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "How does the model represent both factors? Two-way ANOVA represents recovery as an overall mean, two main effects, their interaction, and residual error."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "The two-way ANOVA model"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-next-35-cards-1, ex:l7-next-35-cards-2, ex:l7-next-35-cards-3, ex:l7-next-35-cards-4 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-cards-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Overall and main effects"@en ; cd:body "The overall mean sets the level; method and matrix terms describe average departures."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-cards-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Interaction"@en ; cd:body "The method–matrix term represents departures from additivity."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-cards-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Residual error"@en ; cd:body "Each preparation can differ from its fitted mean for its combination."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-cards-4 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Identify the parameters"@en ; cd:body "Use zero-sum main effects and zero row and column sums for interaction."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-formula a cd:MathExpression ; skos:prefLabel "The two-way ANOVA model"@en ; cd:body "The two-way ANOVA model"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}A\\ast B\\equiv A+B+A{:}B\\\\y_{ijk}=\\mu+\\alpha_i+\\beta_j+(\\alpha\\beta)_{ij}+\\varepsilon_{ijk}\\end{gathered}" ; dct:hasPart ex:l7-next-35-legend ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-next-35-legend-1, ex:l7-next-35-legend-2, ex:l7-next-35-legend-3, ex:l7-next-35-legend-4 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-legend-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Response and indices"@en ; cd:body "$y_{ijk}$ is the recovery (%) of preparation k = 1,…,6 within method i = 1,2,3 (A,B,C) and matrix j = 1,2 (river water, wastewater)."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-legend-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Mean and main effects"@en ; cd:body "$\\mu$ is grand mean recovery (%). $\\alpha_i$ and $\\beta_j$ are the method and matrix main effects in percentage points."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-legend-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Interaction and error"@en ; cd:body "A and B name the method and matrix factors. In model syntax * includes both main effects and the interaction, : specifies the interaction, and ≡ means the formulas include the same terms. The fitted departure from the additive prediction (αβ)ᵢⱼ and the preparation error εᵢⱼₖ are in percentage points."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-35-legend-4 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Operators and conventions"@en ; cd:body "= is equality; + adds effects on the recovery scale. Main effects sum to zero, as do the entries in each row and column of the interaction."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-36-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Build the ANOVA table with interaction"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-36-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "The new interaction row accounts for part of the additive residual."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-36-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Read the two-way ANOVA table"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-next-36-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-36-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Where is interaction tested? The balanced two-way ANOVA separates method, matrix, and interaction, with three effect tests using the common residual mean square."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-next-36-table a cd:TableDefinition ; skos:prefLabel "Balanced 3 × 2 design · Type II ANOVA"@en ; cd:hasTableColumn ex:l7-next-36-table-col-1, ex:l7-next-36-table-col-2, ex:l7-next-36-table-col-3, ex:l7-next-36-table-col-4, ex:l7-next-36-table-col-5, ex:l7-next-36-table-col-6 ; cd:hasTableRow ex:l7-next-36-table-row-1, ex:l7-next-36-table-row-2, ex:l7-next-36-table-row-3, ex:l7-next-36-table-row-4, ex:l7-next-36-table-row-5 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
