  ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "One-way ANOVA"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way-question a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Does preparation method affect recovery?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-intro-concept-01 ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way-item-1, ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way-item-2 ; cd:narration "We start with one factor, preparation method, and one response, recovery. The river-water example gives us three groups of independent preparations. We will use their spread and their mean differences to build the ANOVA."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way-question ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way-heading, ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way-question, ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way, ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way-item-1, ex:l7-scene-chapter-one-way-item-2 .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Post-hoc analysis"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc-question a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Which SPE methods differ within each water matrix?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-24-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc-item-1, ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc-item-2 ; cd:narration "An overall ANOVA can establish evidence that population means differ. We now follow up by comparing specific pairs of means."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc-question ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc-heading, ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc-question, ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc, ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc-item-1, ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc-item-2 .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Two-way ANOVA"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way-question a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "How much of the observed recovery variation is associated with method and matrix?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-30-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way-item-1, ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way-item-2 ; cd:narration "Add wastewater to the experiment so we can compare the same preparation methods in both water matrices. First fit the two factor effects additively, using the same steps as in the one-way ANOVA. Then check how the fit changes when we allow those effects to depend on each other."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way-question ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way-heading, ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way-question, ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way, ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way-item-1, ex:l7-scene-chapter-two-way-item-2 .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Alternatives to classical ANOVA"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives-question a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "What changes when variances differ or the question is about ranks?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-39-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives-item-1, ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives-item-2 ; cd:narration "Start with the scientific question and the independent preparation. For a comparison of means with unequal variances, we can use Welch ANOVA. When we want to compare pooled ranks, Kruskal-Wallis answers a different question."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives-question ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives-heading, ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives-question, ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives, ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives-item-1, ex:l7-scene-chapter-alternatives-item-2 .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Apply what you learned"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice-question a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Which analysis fits each experiment?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-45-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice-item-1, ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice-item-2 ; cd:narration "Use the analytical objective, the experimental units, and the factors to pick a model. We will apply that routine to three cases, then return to the recovery study to summarize what to report."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice-question ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice-heading, ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice-question, ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice, ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice-item-1, ex:l7-scene-chapter-practice-item-2 .
  ex:l7-scene36-additive a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-additive-table-item-1, ex:l7-additive-table-item-2, ex:l7-additive-table-item-3 ; cd:narration "Start with the method and matrix sums of squares and the additive residual. The degrees of freedom count two method shifts and one matrix shift on top of the grand mean. With thirty-six observations, that leaves thirty-two for the residual. Divide each sum of squares by its degrees of freedom to obtain its mean square. The additive residual mean square is 10.5625. Use it as the denominator of both F ratios. Under additivity, these tests ask about the two common factor effects. Eta squared expresses each factor SS as a share of 521: 2.69% for method and 32.44% for water matrix. Why is the share for method so small, and why did its test change from significant to non-significant? Hold that question while we run the same comparison in a second study."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-additive-table-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-additive-table-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-additive-table-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-additive-table ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-additive-table-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-additive-table-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene36-additive, ex:l7-additive-table-item-1, ex:l7-additive-table-item-2, ex:l7-additive-table-item-3 .
  ex:l7-scene36-compare a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-additive-compare-item-1, ex:l7-additive-compare-item-2, ex:l7-additive-compare-item-3 ; cd:narration "Both plots show the same thirty-six observations on the same recovery scale. On the left, group by method and average over both matrices. Method B led at 98 percent in river water alone. Its wastewater mean of 86 percent brings its overall mean down to 92 percent, close to A at 93 and C at 93.5. The method mean square falls from 42 in the one-way analysis to 7 here, while the additive residual mean square is larger, at 10.5625. Together these changes reduce the F ratio from 21 to 0.663. On the right, the two water matrices average 95 and 90.67 percent. To see what the additive ANOVA assumes, look at how it predicts individual recoveries."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-additive-compare-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-additive-compare-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-additive-compare-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-additive-grouped-recoveries ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-additive-compare-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-additive-compare-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene36-compare, ex:l7-additive-compare-item-1, ex:l7-additive-compare-item-2, ex:l7-additive-compare-item-3 .
  ex:l7-scene-operator-assignment a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-30-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-operator-assignment-item-1, ex:l7-operator-assignment-item-2, ex:l7-operator-assignment-item-3 ; cd:narration "We can use an effect size to ask where a lab should look for variation. Imagine that three operators processed the same eighteen river-water samples. X used methods A and B, Y used B and C, and Z used C and A. Each operator processed three separately prepared samples per assigned method. That gives six observations per operator and six per method. For this teaching example, we attach hypothetical operator labels to the existing measurements. In a real study, plan and randomize the sample allocation within the allowed combinations before anyone sees the results."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-operator-assignment-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-operator-assignment-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-operator-assignment-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-operator-design ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-operator-assignment-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-operator-assignment-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-operator-assignment, ex:l7-operator-assignment-item-1, ex:l7-operator-assignment-item-2, ex:l7-operator-assignment-item-3 .
  ex:l7-scene-operator-compare a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-22-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-operator-compare-item-1, ex:l7-operator-compare-item-2, ex:l7-operator-compare-item-3 ; cd:narration "First group the eighteen recoveries by method. About 73.7 percent of observed squared variation lies between those method groups, and the overall p-value is about 0.00004484. Now group the same observations by the hypothetical operators. Their group means account for 18.6 percent of the observed squared variation, with p about 0.214. Notice that X and Y each used method B, while Z used A and C. The operator grouping therefore compares different mixtures of methods. The two eta-squared values describe different groupings of the same observations. To analyze two factors together, we now turn to a design that crosses each preparation method with each water matrix."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-operator-compare-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-operator-compare-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-operator-compare-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-operator-grouping ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-operator-compare-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-operator-compare-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-operator-compare, ex:l7-operator-compare-item-1, ex:l7-operator-compare-item-2, ex:l7-operator-compare-item-3 .
  ex:l7-scene-operator-adjusted a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-operator-adjusted-item-1, ex:l7-operator-adjusted-item-2, ex:l7-operator-adjusted-item-3 ; cd:narration "Fit both factors together and compare each term with a model that already includes the other. Once method is included, adding operator reduces residual sum of squares from 30.00 to 29.88. In this illustrative additive model the adjusted operator p-value is about 0.974 and partial eta squared is 0.4 percent. Method still accounts for 67.8 percent of its effect-plus-residual variation after adjusting for operator. Partial eta squared uses a different denominator from the one-way numbers. These results illustrate how the allocation can produce apparent operator differences. The next chapter develops the two-factor model with a fully crossed design."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-operator-adjusted-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-operator-adjusted-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-operator-adjusted-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-operator-adjusted ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-operator-adjusted-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-operator-adjusted-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-operator-adjusted, ex:l7-operator-adjusted-item-1, ex:l7-operator-adjusted-item-2, ex:l7-operator-adjusted-item-3 .
  ex:l7-scene-model-prediction a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-model-prediction-item-1, ex:l7-model-prediction-item-2, ex:l7-model-prediction-item-3, ex:l7-model-prediction-item-4 ; cd:narration "Return to one of the thirty-six samples. Method B in river water has six measured recoveries. Each dot is one independent preparation. The circled dot is preparation three, measured at 98.06 percent. To predict its recovery, start with 92.83 percent, the mean of all 36 recoveries. Subtract 0.83 percentage points for method B and add 2.17 percentage points for river water. The result is 94.17 percent. All six preparations share that prediction because they use method B and river water. Its residual is the observed recovery minus its fitted value, about 3.89 percentage points. This is the same idea as subtracting a fitted method mean in the one-way example. Now the fitted value comes from two factors. Next, see how the predictions for all six combinations are connected."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-model-prediction-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-model-prediction-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-model-prediction-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-model-prediction ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-model-prediction-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-model-prediction-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-model-prediction-item-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-model-prediction-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-model-prediction, ex:l7-model-prediction-item-1, ex:l7-model-prediction-item-2, ex:l7-model-prediction-item-3, ex:l7-model-prediction-item-4 .
  ex:l7-scene-model-system a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-model-system-item-1, ex:l7-model-system-item-2, ex:l7-model-system-item-3, ex:l7-model-system-item-4 ; cd:narration "Write one equation per method–matrix combination: grand mean plus the shift for that method plus the shift for that matrix. In the two rows shown, both predictions reuse the same grand mean and method B shift. Each water matrix shift is also reused by all three methods. The six equations describe predictions, and the thirty-six measurements inform the same set of parameters. We choose those parameters together to make the sum of squared residuals as small as possible. The shifts are centered around zero to make the grand mean a common reference. Next we check where these shared equations miss the observed pattern."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-model-system-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-model-system-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
