  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-model-system, ex:l7-model-system-item-1, ex:l7-model-system-item-2, ex:l7-model-system-item-3, ex:l7-model-system-item-4 .
  ex:l7-scene-model-pattern a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-model-pattern-item-1, ex:l7-model-pattern-item-2, ex:l7-model-pattern-item-3, ex:l7-model-pattern-item-4 ; cd:narration "Compare methods B and A within the same matrix. In the additive equations the grand mean and the matrix shift cancel when we subtract the two predictions. The fitted gap is therefore minus one percentage point in each matrix. Now reveal the observed gaps. B exceeds A by four points in river water, while B is six points below A in wastewater. These departures go in opposite directions. A single shared method gap cannot follow that pattern. The next example gives this kind of departure a name and shows how it may strengthen or weaken a combined effect."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
