  ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula a cd:MathExpression ; skos:prefLabel "From spread to precision to a weighted mean"@en ; cd:body "From spread to precision to a weighted mean"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{aligned}\\text{Variance of estimated mean:}\\quad &s_i^2/n_i\\\\\\text{Weight (reciprocal):}\\quad &w_i=1/(s_i^2/n_i)=n_i/s_i^2\\\\w_A&=6/3.5\\approx1.714,\\quad w_B=6/56\\approx0.107\\\\\\text{Weighted reference mean:}\\quad &\\bar y_w=\\frac{\\sum_i w_i\\bar y_i}{\\sum_i w_i}\\\\&=\\frac{16(93.5)+1(93)+16(96.5)}{16+1+16}\\%\\approx94.94\\%\\end{aligned}" ; dct:hasPart ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-legend ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula .
  ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-1, ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-2, ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-legend .
  ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Groups and units"@en ; cd:body "i identifies method A, B or C. nᵢ counts independent preparations; sᵢ² is the sample variance of individual recoveries (pp², squared percentage points). Dividing by nᵢ estimates how much the mean would vary across repeat samples of that size. ȳᵢ is the group mean recovery (%)."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-1 .
  ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Weights"@en ; cd:body "wᵢ (pp⁻²) is the reciprocal of that estimated variance: larger groups or tighter observations give the mean more weight. A and C have 16 times B’s weight. The relative weights 16, 1 and 16 give the same weighted mean because their common scale cancels."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-2 .
  ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Test and notation"@en ; cd:body "$\\bar{y}_w$ is the weighted common reference mean (%). Σ adds across A, B and C. Divide the weighted sum of the means by the sum of the weights to return to the recovery scale. Juxtaposition multiplies, + adds, / and fraction bars divide, parentheses group, superscript 2 squares, = denotes equality and ≈ denotes rounding."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-3 .
  ex:l7-teaching-40-example-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Welch ANOVA: work through the weights"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-40-example-heading .
  ex:l7-teaching-40-example-conclusion a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "A and C get sixteen times the weight of B."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-40-example-conclusion .
  ex:l7-teaching-40-example-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Welch ANOVA: work through the weights"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-teaching-40-example-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-40-example-focus .
  ex:l7-teaching-40-example-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "With six preparations each, A and C carry 16 times the weight of B because their means are estimated more precisely."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-40-example-definition .
  ex:level7-anova-kw-rank-sums a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Kruskal–Wallis: the evidence is in the rank sums"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-kw-rank-sums.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Rank sums are 3.5, 6.5 and 11.0. Correcting for tied ranks gives H 4.191. Of 90 equally likely allocations with two per group, 12 are as extreme, so exact p is 0.133."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-kw-rank-sums .
  ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula a cd:MathExpression ; skos:prefLabel "Rank sums, ties and the reference"@en ; cd:body "Rank sums, ties and the reference"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{aligned}H_{\\rm raw}&=\\frac{12}{N(N+1)}\\sum_{i=1}^{k}\\frac{R_i^2}{n_i}-3(N+1)\\\\C&=1-\\frac{\\sum_j(t_j^3-t_j)}{N^3-N},& H&=H_{\\rm raw}/C\\end{aligned}" ; dct:hasPart ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula-legend ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula .
  ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula-symbol-1, ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula-symbol-2, ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula-symbol-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula-legend .
  ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula-symbol-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Ranks and counts"@en ; cd:body "Rᵢ is group i's pooled rank sum; nᵢ is its sample size; N = 6 is the total, and k = 3 is the group count. tⱼ is the number of values in tied set j."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula-symbol-1 .
  ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula-symbol-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Statistic"@en ; cd:body "$H_{\\mathrm{raw}}$ is the uncorrected statistic, C is the tie correction, and H is the dimensionless corrected statistic."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula-symbol-2 .
  ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula-symbol-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Operations and reference"@en ; cd:body "Σ sums over groups or tied sets; fractions divide, powers 2 and 3 square and cube, parentheses group terms, juxtaposition multiplies, and +, −, = denote addition, subtraction and equality. Exact p counts equally likely label allocations at least as extreme under exchangeability."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula-symbol-3 .
  ex:l7-teaching-41-example-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Kruskal–Wallis: from ranks to the test"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-41-example-heading .
  ex:l7-teaching-41-example-conclusion a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "The exact rank test gives p = 0.133."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-41-example-conclusion .
  ex:l7-teaching-41-example-focus a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Kruskal–Wallis: from ranks to the test"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l7-teaching-41-example-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-41-example-focus .
  ex:l7-teaching-41-example-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "The tied ranks give H = 4.191; the exact test gives p = 0.133 for this small example."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-41-example-definition .
  ex:level7-anova-manova-pairs a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Several responses, one experimental factor"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-manova-pairs.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "The paired recoveries of two analytes for each of six independent preparations in each SPE method. Mean vectors: A (90,87), B (94,89), C (92,94), in percent."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-manova-pairs .
