<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/level7-anova-continuation> {
  ex:level7-anova-visual-20 a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Where independent replication comes from"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-visual-20.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Three separately prepared vials provide three independent units. Three injections of one extract provide three technical repeats of one unit."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-visual-20 .
  ex:level7-anova-visual-23 a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Report the test, effect size and scope"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-visual-23.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "One-way ANOVA for three methods with six independent preparations each. The overall test gives F 21 with 2 and 15 degrees of freedom, p about 0.00004484. The fitted method means account for 73.7 percent of observed squared variation. Compare individual effects with analytical tolerances."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-visual-23 .
  ex:level7-anova-visual-24 a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "The global decision leaves the pairs open"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-visual-24.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "All three pairwise method comparisons form one family. Family-wise error is the chance of at least one false positive in that family. Tukey accounts for the whole family."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-visual-24 .
  ex:level7-anova-visual-25 a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "One family of three comparisons"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-visual-25.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Three schematic experiments each draw six preparations per method from populations with the same mean of 95 percent. The largest observed sample-mean gap is 0.8 percentage points between A and B, then 1.5 between A and C, then 0.9 between B and C. Repeating this process yields the null distribution of the largest gap after scaling by the estimated standard error."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-visual-25 .
  ex:level7-anova-visual-28 a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Which follow-up fits the comparison?"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-visual-28.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Three two-sided pooled t-tests have raw p-values 0.000112 for B versus C, 0.000624 for B versus A, and 0.24874 for A versus C. In that order, Holm multiplies by 3, 2 and 1, then takes the running maximum capped at 1. Adjusted p-values are 0.000336, 0.001248 and 0.24874."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-visual-28 .
  ex:level7-anova-visual-39 a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Choose by design, target and error model"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-visual-39.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Check independent experimental units. For one factor, ordinary ANOVA compares means with a common variance, Welch compares means with unequal variances, and Kruskal–Wallis addresses a rank-based question."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-visual-39 .
  ex:level7-anova-welch-weights a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Welch gives more influence to a more precise mean"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-welch-weights.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "All three methods have six independent preparations. For A and C, 6 divided by sample variance 3.5 gives weight 1.714 each. For B, 6 divided by 56 gives weight 0.107, one sixteenth as much. With relative weights 16, 1 and 16, the common reference mean is 94.94 percent. Welch F is 3.786 with approximate degrees of freedom 2 and 9.06, giving p 0.064."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:level7-anova-welch-weights .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/media/level7-anova-model-checklist> {
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/level7-anova-model-checklist> a <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/MediaAsset> ; <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Four questions for an ANOVA report"@en ;
    <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/uri> "/chemometrics/level7-anova-model-checklist.svg"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> ; <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/mediaType> "image/svg+xml" ;
    <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/alternativeText> "A checklist for interpreting ANOVA. Identify factors and independent units, fit means and separate residual variation, evaluate the F ratio, then report effect size, diagnostics and follow-up."@en ; <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> true ; <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/supportsResource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/level7-anova-model-checklist> .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/level7-anova-continuation> {
  ex:l7-treatment-transition-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "A second example"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-transition-statement a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Why did the evidence for a method effect change? Let’s compare it with a second experiment."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-treatment-transition-heading, ex:l7-treatment-transition-statement .
  ex:l7-treatment-observations-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Does the water treatment technique matter?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-observations-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Use the measurements under NOM addition for the first comparison."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-treatment-observations a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Does the water treatment technique matter?"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-treatment-observations.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "In the illustrative NOM condition the measured removals are activated carbon 51, 55, 54, 56%; ultrafiltration 62, 66, 65, 67%; ion exchange 69, 73, 71, 75%."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-treatment-observations-heading, ex:level7-anova-treatment-observations, ex:l7-treatment-observations-takeaway .
  ex:l7-treatment-one-way-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Build the one-way treatment ANOVA table"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-one-way-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Under NOM addition, mean removal differs among the techniques."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-treatment-one-way a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Build the one-way treatment ANOVA table"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-treatment-one-way.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "One-way ANOVA using the 12 NOM runs. The technique test is significant at the five percent level."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-treatment-one-way-heading, ex:level7-anova-treatment-one-way, ex:l7-treatment-one-way-takeaway .
  ex:l7-treatment-design-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Add a second factor to the treatment study"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-design-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Three techniques × three water conditions gives nine combinations."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-treatment-design a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Add a second factor to the treatment study"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-treatment-design.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "The crossed design has 36 independent runs, four per combination. Activated carbon, NOM addition: 51, 55, 54, 56%. Ultrafiltration, NOM addition: 62, 66, 65, 67%. Ion exchange, NOM addition: 69, 73, 71, 75%. Activated carbon, Phosphate addition: 58, 63, 61, 62%. Ultrafiltration, Phosphate addition: 68, 74, 71, 75%. Ion exchange, Phosphate addition: 76, 80, 77, 79%. Activated carbon, Ozone pretreatment: 68, 74, 70, 72%. Ultrafiltration, Ozone pretreatment: 76, 79, 78, 79%. Ion exchange, Ozone pretreatment: 88, 90, 86, 88%."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-treatment-design-heading, ex:level7-anova-treatment-design, ex:l7-treatment-design-takeaway .
  ex:l7-treatment-two-way-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Build the additive treatment ANOVA table"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-two-way-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Both technique and water condition are significant in the additive model."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-treatment-two-way a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Build the additive treatment ANOVA table"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-treatment-two-way.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Additive ANOVA for water treatment. Both the technique and condition tests are significant at the five percent level."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-treatment-two-way-heading, ex:level7-anova-treatment-two-way, ex:l7-treatment-two-way-takeaway .
  ex:l7-four-tables-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Why does the conclusion change in only one study?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-four-tables-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "The one-way test compares means in one condition. The additive model compares means averaged across conditions."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-four-tables a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Why does the conclusion change in only one study?"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-four-tables.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Four ANOVA tables compare SPE recovery under river water alone and across both matrices, and removal under natural organic matter alone and across all conditions. A check mark indicates p below 0.05. A cross marks the SPE method in the additive model, with p = 0.522."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-four-tables-heading, ex:level7-anova-four-tables, ex:l7-four-tables-takeaway .
  ex:l7-compare-patterns-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "How do the gaps between group means change?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-compare-patterns-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "The treatment gaps stay roughly constant across conditions. The recovery gaps change, and some method rankings reverse."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-compare-patterns a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "How do the gaps between group means change?"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-compare-patterns.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Stage one shows three technique profiles across ozone pretreatment, NOM addition and phosphate addition. The gaps vary while the rank order stays stable. Stage two shows crossing SPE profiles from wastewater to river water."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-compare-patterns-heading, ex:level7-anova-compare-patterns, ex:l7-compare-patterns-takeaway .
  ex:l7-interaction-meaning-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Is the change in group gaps larger than we would expect from scatter?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-meaning-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Changing gaps suggest interaction. Sampling uncertainty determines how strongly the data support it."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-interaction-meaning a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "When one factor changes the effect of another"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-interaction-meaning.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Plant growth in centimetres is compared with and without added nutrients. Blue denotes adequate water and purple limited water. Widening or narrowing gaps illustrate synergy or antagonism for this specified nutrient response under different water supplies. Illustrative confidence intervals show uncertainty. The interaction test assesses whether the gaps change beyond sampling variation."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-interaction-meaning-heading, ex:level7-anova-interaction-meaning, ex:l7-interaction-meaning-takeaway .
  ex:l7-interaction-model-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Where does the interaction sum of squares come from?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-model-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "The interaction explains part of the additive residual."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-interaction-model a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Where does the interaction sum of squares come from?"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-interaction-model.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "In the SPE study, the additive model assigns 14 to method, 169 to matrix and 338 to residuals. Adding the interaction splits 338 into 278 for method by matrix and 60 for the remaining residual. Total sum of squares stays at 521."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-model-formula a cd:MathExpression ; skos:prefLabel "Interaction in a balanced design"@en ; cd:body "Interaction in a balanced design"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{aligned}\n\\bar y_{ij\\cdot}&=\\frac{1}{r}\\sum_{k=1}^{r}y_{ijk}\\\\\nd_{ij}&=\\underbrace{\\bar y_{ij\\cdot}}_{\\text{mean for the combination}}-\\underbrace{\\Bigl(\\overbrace{\\bar y_{i\\cdot\\cdot}}^{\\text{factor A mean}}+\\overbrace{\\bar y_{\\cdot j\\cdot}}^{\\text{factor B mean}}-\\overbrace{\\bar y_{\\cdot\\cdot\\cdot}}^{\\text{grand mean}}\\Bigr)}_{\\text{reference from the factor means}}\\\\\nSS_{AB}&=r\\sum_{i=1}^{a}\\sum_{j=1}^{b}d_{ij}^{2}=SS_{\\mathrm{res,add}}-SS_W\\\\\nSS_T&=SS_A+SS_B+SS_{AB}+SS_W\n\\\\r&=\\frac{N}{ab},\\qquad \\text{SPE: }r=\\frac{36}{3\\times 2}=6\n\\end{aligned}" ; dct:hasPart ex:l7-interaction-model-legend ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-model-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-interaction-model-symbols ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-model-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and units"@en ; cd:body "- **$i$, $j$**: Levels of factors A and B that identify a combination.\n- **$\\bar y_{ij\\cdot}$**: Observed mean for one combination. $y_{ijk}$ is recovery for preparation $k$ in that combination. A bar denotes a mean and a dot pools the corresponding index.\n- **$\\bar y_{i\\cdot\\cdot}$, $\\bar y_{\\cdot j\\cdot}$**: Means across all runs at the indicated level of A or B.\n- **$\\bar y_{\\cdot\\cdot\\cdot}$**: Overall mean of all runs. The means are expressed in percent.\n- **$d_{ij}$**: Gap between the observed mean and its reference from the factor means, in percentage points.\n- **$a$, $b$**: Numbers of levels of factors A and B, respectively.\n- **$r$**: Number of independent runs per combination. Each combination has the same run count. In the SPE example, $r=6$.\n- **$N$**: Total number of independent runs across all $ab$ combinations. Divide by $ab$ to get $r$.\n- **$SS_T$, $SS_A$, $SS_B$**: Total sum of squares and sums of squares for the two factors.\n- **$SS_{AB}$, $SS_W$**: Interaction sum of squares and remaining residual sum of squares. $SS_{\\mathrm{res,add}}$ is the residual sum of squares in the additive model. All sums of squares are in squared percentage points.\n- **$\\sum$, $+,-,=,{}^2$**: Add across the indicated levels, add, subtract, equality and square. The multiplier $r$ weights each squared gap by its run count.\n\nThe formulas use a balanced design with the same number of runs for every combination."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-interaction-model-heading, ex:level7-anova-interaction-model, ex:l7-interaction-model-takeaway, ex:l7-interaction-model-formula, ex:l7-interaction-model-legend, ex:l7-interaction-model-symbols .
  ex:l7-interaction-worked-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Calculate the interaction sum of squares"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-interaction-worked a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Calculate the interaction sum of squares"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-interaction-worked.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Four steps use the SPE observations. Average six river-water recoveries for method B to get 98 percent. The additive reference is 94.17 percent and the deviation is about 3.83 percentage points. Use all six method and matrix combinations to get interaction SS 278. Subtract 278 from the additive residual 338 to leave 60."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-worked-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "The six weighted squared gaps account for 278 of the 338 additive residual."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-interaction-worked-heading, ex:level7-anova-interaction-worked, ex:l7-interaction-worked-takeaway .
  ex:l7-interaction-test-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Build and test the interaction row in both studies"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-test-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "SPE shows interaction, so compare methods within each matrix. The treatment study gives insufficient evidence of interaction."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-interaction-test a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Build and test the interaction row in both studies"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-interaction-test.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Both ANOVA tables show eta squared as the share of total sums of squares. SPE: method 2.69%, matrix 32.44%, interaction 53.36% (p = 5.4767e-12). Water treatment: technique 53.38%, condition 41.82%, interaction 0.79% (p = 0.28653). The SPE method is marked at 2.69% on a scale with rough benchmarks of 1% (small), 6% (medium), and 14% (large)."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-interaction-test-heading, ex:level7-anova-interaction-test, ex:l7-interaction-test-takeaway .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/scenes/level7-anova-continuation> {
  ex:l7-scene-chapter-treatment a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-treatment-transition-item-1, ex:l7-treatment-transition-item-2 ; cd:narration "To understand what happened in the two-way ANOVA, let's look at a different example."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-transition-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-treatment-transition-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-transition-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-treatment-transition-statement ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-chapter-treatment, ex:l7-treatment-transition-item-1, ex:l7-treatment-transition-item-2 .
  ex:l7-scene-treatment-observations dct:subject ex:slide-topic-use-case .
  ex:l7-treatment-observations-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-treatment-observations-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-observations-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-treatment-observations ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-observations-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-treatment-observations-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-treatment-observations a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-treatment-observations-item-1, ex:l7-treatment-observations-item-2, ex:l7-treatment-observations-item-3 ; cd:narration "Start a separate teaching example with three water treatment techniques. In this first comparison, every run uses water with the same addition of natural organic matter, abbreviated NOM. Measure the percentage of a target contaminant removed in four independent runs for each technique. Each dot represents a separate run. The group means are 54, 65 and 72 percent. The graph suggests a difference, so the next step is to ask whether the separation is large compared with the scatter inside each technique."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-treatment-observations, ex:l7-treatment-observations-item-1, ex:l7-treatment-observations-item-2, ex:l7-treatment-observations-item-3 .
  ex:l7-treatment-one-way-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-treatment-one-way-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-one-way-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-treatment-one-way ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-one-way-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-treatment-one-way-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-treatment-one-way a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-treatment-one-way-item-1, ex:l7-treatment-one-way-item-2, ex:l7-treatment-one-way-item-3 ; cd:narration "Work through the table exactly as in the first example. First partition total variation into variation between techniques and variation within a technique. Then count degrees of freedom. Three techniques give two between-technique degrees of freedom, and twelve observations leave nine within-technique degrees of freedom. Divide each sum of squares by its degrees of freedom and compare the mean squares with the F ratio. The p-value is below 0.05. Under the NOM condition, at least one technique has a different mean removal."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-treatment-one-way, ex:l7-treatment-one-way-item-1, ex:l7-treatment-one-way-item-2, ex:l7-treatment-one-way-item-3 .
  ex:l7-treatment-design-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-treatment-design-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-design-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-treatment-design ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-design-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-treatment-design-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-treatment-design a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-treatment-design-item-1, ex:l7-treatment-design-item-2, ex:l7-treatment-design-item-3 ; cd:narration "Now extend the study by crossing each treatment technique with three water conditions. One condition adds natural organic matter, one adds phosphate and one uses ozone pretreatment. These are three mutually exclusive levels of a single factor. A run has exactly one condition and exactly one technique. Each of the nine combinations has four independent runs. Keep the twelve NOM runs from the one-way comparison as the first column. The other two columns extend the comparison to the additional conditions."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-treatment-design, ex:l7-treatment-design-item-1, ex:l7-treatment-design-item-2, ex:l7-treatment-design-item-3 .
  ex:l7-treatment-two-way-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-treatment-two-way-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-two-way-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-treatment-two-way ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-treatment-two-way-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-treatment-two-way-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-treatment-two-way a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-treatment-two-way-item-1, ex:l7-treatment-two-way-item-2, ex:l7-treatment-two-way-item-3 ; cd:narration "Use all thirty-six runs. The additive table has one row for the technique and another row for the water condition. Both factors have three levels, so each gets two degrees of freedom. The remaining thirty-one degrees of freedom belong to the residual. Divide both factor mean squares by the same residual mean square. At the five percent level, both technique and water condition are significant in this model. The evidence for a technique effect remains after adding the second factor."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-treatment-two-way, ex:l7-treatment-two-way-item-1, ex:l7-treatment-two-way-item-2, ex:l7-treatment-two-way-item-3 .
  ex:l7-four-tables-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-four-tables-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-four-tables-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-four-tables ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-four-tables-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-four-tables-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-four-tables a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-four-tables-item-1, ex:l7-four-tables-item-2, ex:l7-four-tables-item-3 ; cd:narration "Read across the two rows. The first example asks about SPE method. It shows a clear method result in river water alone and no statistically significant common method effect when both matrices enter the additive model. The second example asks about treatment technique. It shows a clear technique result in the NOM runs and still shows a clear technique result when all water conditions enter the model. Both one-way tables use the reference condition shown in the earlier slides. What differs in the data?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-four-tables, ex:l7-four-tables-item-1, ex:l7-four-tables-item-2, ex:l7-four-tables-item-3 .
  ex:l7-compare-patterns-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-compare-patterns-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-compare-patterns-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-compare-patterns ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-compare-patterns-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-compare-patterns-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-compare-patterns a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-compare-patterns-item-1, ex:l7-compare-patterns-item-2, ex:l7-compare-patterns-item-3 ; cd:narration "Start with the treatment data. Each line joins the means for a single technique, one point per condition. The horizontal axis lists categories. The connecting lines help compare the gaps, which vary a little while the techniques keep the same order. Then switch to the SPE data. Method B is four percentage points above A in river water and six percentage points below A in wastewater. The lines cross. The method difference changes with the matrix, so averaging over matrices can hide a strong difference within an individual matrix."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-compare-patterns, ex:l7-compare-patterns-item-1, ex:l7-compare-patterns-item-2, ex:l7-compare-patterns-item-3 .
  ex:l7-interaction-meaning-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-interaction-meaning-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-meaning-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-interaction-meaning ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-meaning-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-interaction-meaning-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-interaction-meaning a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-interaction-meaning-item-1, ex:l7-interaction-meaning-item-2, ex:l7-interaction-meaning-item-3 ; cd:narration "Each plot shows plant growth with and without added nutrients. Blue represents adequate water and purple represents limited water. Compare the nutrient response under the two water supplies. On the left, the response to nutrients is larger with adequate water, illustrating synergy for this growth comparison. On the right, the combined response falls below the additive expectation, illustrating antagonism in this example. In the middle, the gaps are nearly constant. Sample means fluctuate, and the confidence intervals illustrate uncertainty. Use the interaction test to assess whether the changing gaps exceed what we would expect from sampling variation."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-interaction-meaning, ex:l7-interaction-meaning-item-1, ex:l7-interaction-meaning-item-2, ex:l7-interaction-meaning-item-3 .
  ex:l7-interaction-model-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-interaction-model-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-model-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-interaction-model ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-model-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-interaction-model-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-model-item-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-interaction-model-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-interaction-model a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-interaction-model-item-1, ex:l7-interaction-model-item-2, ex:l7-interaction-model-item-3, ex:l7-interaction-model-item-4 ; cd:narration "Start with the additive model for SPE recovery. Method and water matrix account for the first two parts. The rest is residual variation in that model. Adding method by matrix lets the model describe differences specific to combinations of method and water matrix. In this balanced design the main-effect sums of squares stay the same. The additive residual splits into 278 for the interaction and 60 that remain unexplained. The total stays 521. The formula tab shows how to calculate the split, and the next slide works it out from the measurements."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-interaction-model, ex:l7-interaction-model-item-1, ex:l7-interaction-model-item-2, ex:l7-interaction-model-item-3, ex:l7-interaction-model-item-4 .
  ex:l7-interaction-worked-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-interaction-worked-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-worked-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-interaction-worked ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-worked-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-interaction-worked-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-interaction-worked a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-interaction-worked-item-1, ex:l7-interaction-worked-item-2, ex:l7-interaction-worked-item-3 ; cd:narration "Start with the six measured recoveries for method B in river water. Add them and divide by six to get ninety-eight percent. The additive reference combines the method and matrix means and subtracts the grand mean once. Subtract this reference from the observed mean to get a gap of about 3.83 percentage points. Repeat for all six combinations. Square each gap and multiply by six because there are six preparations in each combination. Add the six contributions using the unrounded values. The interaction sum of squares is 278, leaving 60 of the original 338 residual sum of squares."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-interaction-worked, ex:l7-interaction-worked-item-1, ex:l7-interaction-worked-item-2, ex:l7-interaction-worked-item-3 .
  ex:l7-interaction-test-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-interaction-test-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-test-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-interaction-test ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-interaction-test-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-interaction-test-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-interaction-test a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-29-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-interaction-test-item-1, ex:l7-interaction-test-item-2, ex:l7-interaction-test-item-3 ; cd:narration "Start with the additive residual in each study. Split it into variation assigned to the interaction and variation left as residual error. The interaction uses two degrees of freedom in the SPE example and four in the treatment example. The interaction accounts for 53.36 percent of total variation in the SPE example and 0.79 percent in the treatment example. For each study, divide the interaction mean square by the remaining residual mean square and read the p-value. At the five percent level we detect interaction for SPE recovery. The treatment example provides no significant evidence of interaction. That matches the contrast between crossing lines and profiles with smaller changes in their gaps."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-interaction-test, ex:l7-interaction-test-item-1, ex:l7-interaction-test-item-2, ex:l7-interaction-test-item-3 .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/level7-anova-continuation> {
  ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-tukey a cd:MediaAsset ; cd:uri "https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/prc/section4/prc471.htm"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "text/html" ; cd:alternativeText "NIST Tukey HSD"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-tukey .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-q-table a cd:MediaAsset ; cd:uri "https://faculty.washington.edu/heagerty/Books/Biostatistics/TABLES/StudentizedRange/"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "text/html" ; cd:alternativeText "Studentized range critical values"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-q-table .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-q-distribution a cd:MediaAsset ; cd:uri "https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/Tukey.html"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "text/html" ; cd:alternativeText "Studentized range distribution"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-q-distribution .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-r-tukey a cd:MediaAsset ; cd:uri "https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/TukeyHSD.html"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "text/html" ; cd:alternativeText "R Tukey HSD and simultaneous intervals"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-r-tukey .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "ANOVA found a difference. Where is it?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-opener a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "ANOVA found a difference. Where is it?"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-post-hoc-opener.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "A significant ANOVA gives evidence that at least one population mean differs. Many post-hoc procedures exist. Tukey HSD compares every pair of group means."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "ANOVA tests all means together. Post-hoc analysis identifies which pairs differ."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-heading, ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-opener, ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-takeaway .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Compare each gap with the HSD"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-rule a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Compare each gap with the HSD"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-post-hoc-rule.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Three analytical methods have five measurements each, with means 10, 12 and 17 mg/L. With an HSD of approximately 3.4 mg/L, C differs from A and B. The A–B result is inconclusive."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "An absolute mean gap larger than the HSD is statistically significant."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-heading, ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-rule, ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-takeaway .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-hsd-formula a cd:MathExpression ; skos:prefLabel "Tukey HSD for equal group sizes"@en ; cd:body "Tukey HSD for equal group sizes"@en ; cd:latex "\\mathrm{HSD}=q_{\\mathrm{crit}}\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{MS}_E}{n}}" ; dct:hasPart ex:l7-post-hoc-hsd-legend ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-hsd-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-post-hoc-hsd-symbols ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-hsd-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and units"@en ; cd:body "- **$HSD$**: The minimum absolute difference for significance, in the same units as the response.\n- **$q_{crit}$**: The dimensionless upper critical value of the studentized range for the number of group means, the residual degrees of freedom, and the chosen familywise significance level.\n- **$MS_E$**: The residual mean square from ANOVA, in squared response units.\n- **$n$**: The common number of independent observations per group.\n- **Operations**: The fraction divides the residual mean square by the group size. The square root restores the response units and multiplication by the critical value gives the cutoff."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-hsd-formula, ex:l7-post-hoc-hsd-legend, ex:l7-post-hoc-hsd-symbols .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Where does the Tukey cutoff come from?"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-cutoff a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Where does the Tukey cutoff come from?"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-post-hoc-cutoff.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "The critical value is the 95th percentile of the studentized range distribution for three groups and 12 error degrees of freedom. With error mean square 4 and five observations per group, Tukey HSD is approximately 3.37 mg/L."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "More within-group scatter raises the cutoff. More observations lower it at fixed scatter."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-heading, ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-cutoff, ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-takeaway .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-family-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Keep all pairwise comparisons in one family"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-family a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Keep all pairwise comparisons in one family"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-post-hoc-family.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Tukey controls the chance of one or more false positives in the comparison family at five percent under the classical assumptions. A Tukey-adjusted p-value can be compared directly with 0.05."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-family-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "A simultaneous Tukey interval that excludes zero identifies a significant pair."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-family-heading, ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-family, ex:l7-post-hoc-family-takeaway .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "SPE recovery: compare methods within each matrix"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-spe a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "SPE recovery: compare methods within each matrix"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-post-hoc-spe.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "One Tukey plot compares six intervals on a shared axis, with river water and wastewater paired for each method contrast. Each matrix is a separate 95% family. Both use the full model residual MSE of 2 and 30 error degrees of freedom. River water: HSD 2.01 percentage points. A versus B, adjusted p 8.978e-05. A versus C, adjusted p 0.4482. B versus C, adjusted p 2.902e-06. Wastewater: HSD 2.01 percentage points. A versus B, adjusted p 1.029e-07. A versus C, adjusted p 0.05175. B versus C, adjusted p 2.185e-10."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Within each matrix, A–B and B–C differ. A–C remains inconclusive, and equivalence requires a separate test."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-heading, ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-spe, ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-takeaway .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-heading a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Water treatment: compare techniques across conditions"@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-treatment a cd:MediaAsset ; skos:prefLabel "Water treatment: compare techniques across conditions"@en ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level7-anova-post-hoc-treatment.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Use the additive model to compare marginal means averaged equally over the three conditions. AC is activated carbon, UF ultrafiltration and IX ion exchange. Use the additive model MSE and 31 error degrees of freedom. Average over the three water conditions: HSD 2.30 percentage points. AC versus UF, adjusted p 4.305e-11. AC versus IX, adjusted p 5.329e-15. UF versus IX, adjusted p 8.704e-09."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-takeaway a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "All three technique pairs differ in mean removal in the additive model."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-heading, ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-treatment, ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-takeaway .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/scenes/level7-anova-continuation> {
  ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-opener ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-item-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-tukey ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-post-hoc-opener a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-24-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-item-1, ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-item-2, ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-item-3, ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-item-4 ; cd:narration "A significant ANOVA gives evidence that at least one population mean differs. Many post-hoc procedures exist. Tukey HSD compares every pair of group means. Start with the global question about the population means. If the overall test is significant, you still need a comparison that targets the differences you want to understand. In the next slides, we will consider three analytical methods and ask which pairs separate clearly. Tukey HSD is particularly useful when every pair is of interest and we want to interpret the comparisons together."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-post-hoc-opener, ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-item-1, ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-item-2, ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-item-3, ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-item-4 .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-rule ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-item-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-tukey ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-post-hoc-rule a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-24-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-item-1, ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-item-2, ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-item-3, ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-item-4 ; cd:narration "Three analytical methods have five measurements each, with means 10, 12 and 17 mg/L. With an HSD of approximately 3.4 mg/L, C differs from A and B. The A–B result is inconclusive. First take the absolute difference so that the order of subtraction does not affect the decision. The gap of two is below the cutoff. The gaps of seven and five are above it, so method C differs from both other methods at this level. The smaller gap remains inconclusive. The next slide shows how the cutoff follows from the estimated error variance."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-post-hoc-rule, ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-item-1, ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-item-2, ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-item-3, ex:l7-post-hoc-rule-item-4 .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-math-item a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-hsd-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-cutoff ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 5 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-q-table ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-5 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 6 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-q-distribution ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-post-hoc-cutoff a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-24-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-math-item, ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-1, ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-2, ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-3, ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-4, ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-5 ; cd:narration "The critical value is the 95th percentile of the studentized range distribution for three groups and 12 error degrees of freedom. With error mean square 4 and five observations per group, Tukey HSD is approximately 3.37 mg/L. The distribution describes the range between the largest and smallest of the group means under the equal-means null, scaled by the estimated standard error. This is why its quantile depends on how many group means are in the family. Find three groups across the table and twelve residual degrees of freedom down the table to read 3.77 at the five percent level."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-math-item, ex:l7-scene-post-hoc-cutoff, ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-1, ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-2, ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-3, ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-4, ex:l7-post-hoc-cutoff-item-5 .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-family-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-family-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-family-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-family ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-family-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-family-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-family-item-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-r-tukey ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-post-hoc-family a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-24-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-post-hoc-family-item-1, ex:l7-post-hoc-family-item-2, ex:l7-post-hoc-family-item-3, ex:l7-post-hoc-family-item-4 ; cd:narration "Tukey controls the chance of one or more false positives in the comparison family at five percent under the classical assumptions. A Tukey-adjusted p-value can be compared directly with 0.05. With multiple pairs, the error of interest is getting even one false positive in the family. Tukey handles the comparisons jointly. On a Tukey plot, the point gives the signed difference in means and the line shows its simultaneous confidence interval. Check the vertical line at zero. If the interval crosses zero, the evidence is insufficient for that pair at the chosen level."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-post-hoc-family, ex:l7-post-hoc-family-item-1, ex:l7-post-hoc-family-item-2, ex:l7-post-hoc-family-item-3, ex:l7-post-hoc-family-item-4 .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-spe ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-item-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-r-tukey ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-post-hoc-spe a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-24-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-item-1, ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-item-2, ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-item-3, ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-item-4 ; cd:narration "One Tukey plot compares six intervals on a shared axis, with river water and wastewater paired for each method contrast. Each matrix is a separate 95% family. Both use the full model residual MSE of 2 and 30 error degrees of freedom. River water: HSD 2.01 percentage points. A versus B, adjusted p 8.978e-05. A versus C, adjusted p 0.4482. B versus C, adjusted p 2.902e-06. Wastewater: HSD 2.01 percentage points. A versus B, adjusted p 1.029e-07. A versus C, adjusted p 0.05175. B versus C, adjusted p 2.185e-10. The method ranking changes with the water matrix, so read the method comparisons within each matrix. The adjusted p-values protect the three contrasts within each matrix. In river water, method B has the highest mean. In wastewater it has the lowest. Check whether the intervals for the two contrasts involving method B cross zero, then compare that with the A versus C result."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-post-hoc-spe, ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-item-1, ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-item-2, ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-item-3, ex:l7-post-hoc-spe-item-4 .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-treatment ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-item-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-r-tukey ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-scene-post-hoc-treatment a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-next-24-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-item-1, ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-item-2, ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-item-3, ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-item-4 ; cd:narration "Use the additive model to compare marginal means averaged equally over the three conditions. AC is activated carbon, UF ultrafiltration and IX ion exchange. Use the additive model MSE and 31 error degrees of freedom. Average over the three water conditions: HSD 2.30 percentage points. AC versus UF, adjusted p 4.305e-11. AC versus IX, adjusted p 5.329e-15. UF versus IX, adjusted p 8.704e-09. Here we compare marginal means from the additive model using all three water conditions with equal weight. Each technique contributes twelve observations to its mean. The three simultaneous intervals lie entirely on one side of zero, so each of the three pairs shows evidence of a difference. The signed differences follow the row and column order used in the plot."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene-post-hoc-treatment, ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-item-1, ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-item-2, ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-item-3, ex:l7-post-hoc-treatment-item-4 .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/paths/level7-anova-intro-review> {
  ex:path-level7-anova-intro-review cd:hasStep ex:l7-scene-chapter-post-hoc-step .
  ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-step a cd:PathStep ; cd:position 45 ; cd:usesScene ex:l7-scene-post-hoc-opener ; cd:usesResource ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-heading, ex:level7-anova-post-hoc-opener, ex:l7-post-hoc-opener-takeaway, ex:l7-post-hoc-ref-tukey ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
